{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood","id":1529766,"title":"[WIR] Children of the Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-31T13:13:33-08:00","id":1529766,"title":"[WIR] Children of the Blood","content":"I've mentioned it elsewhere but I genuinely love Onyx Path Publishing's take on<i> Vampire: The Masquerade</i> Fifth Edition. More than anyone, I feel they had a clear and consistent vision for what the game was about and how to marry ease of access for new players with a fidelity to the lore that came before. So, obviously, I was going to try to do as many of their books as possible. This one is going to be about CHILDREN OF THE BLOOD.<br /> <br /> I hope people will read along with me and share their opinions on the subject.<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/18205/351521.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/18205/351521.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1vzi28wh99zvq.cloudfront.net/images/18205/351521.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <u>Articles</u><br /> <br /> Note: Due to the changing nature of the forum and how it functions, we'll no longer be updating the opening post with the articles of the book's links. The book will be handled in a chronological fashion from beginning to end, though, so feel free to just go through the various pages of this thread to find the relevant articles.<br /> <br /> <u>WIR Links</u><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356870-wir-anarchs-unbound-anarchy-in-the-wod\">Anarchs Unbound</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1323475-wir-beckett-s-jyhad-diary-the-big-book-of-metaplot\">Beckett's Jyhad Diary</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281406-wir-chicago-by-night-5th-edition\">Chicago by Night 5th Edition</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388414-v5-wir-the-chicago-folios-and-let-the-streets-run-red\">The Chicago Folios</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods\">Cults of the Blood Gods</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1316615-wir-the-gary-chronicles-forged-in-steel-ashes-to-ashes-dust-to-dust-etc\">The Gary Chronicles</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437162-wir-let-the-streets-run-red-complete\">Let the Streets Run Red</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1351194-wir-project-twilight-a-werewolf-book-now-very-useful-for-vampires\">Project: Twilight</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-01-2024, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T17:45:47-08:00","id":1529785,"title":"","content":"Lots of topics to choose from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T17:59:52-08:00","id":1529787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529785#post1529785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of topics to choose from.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan is just to go over each and every individual character and say what I liked and disliked about them. I'm biased because I actually created a couple of characters here for the Kickstarter but the good folk at OPP make them better.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T20:22:41-08:00","id":1529798,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of the Blood part 1</b><br /> <br /> <i>Children of the Blood</i> comes from the long tradition of books like <i>Children of the Inquisition</i>, <i>Children of the Night</i>, and <i>Children of the Revolution</i>. They are NPCs that are usually tied to a specific place but can be inserted anywhere. Generally, these books are some of the most informative of the books. We learned much about the origins of the Camarilla from Rafael de Corazon's biography. We got a lot out of Dracula's backstory. We figured out how the function of the Camarilla military occurred from Karsh's write-up.<br /> <br /> COTB seems to be far more on the lower end of the power scale. Part of what 5th Edition has laser focused on the idea that the power level of V:TM was way too high in previous editions. I think this is a smart move but you need to have a balance between the powerful Elder types and the incredibly weak ones. After all, coteries tend to gang up on their enemies when and if they decide to attack someone.<br /> <br /> I'm very excited about these as I think V:TM is primarily a social game and every single character is a potential series of adventures by themselves. Most of these NPCs are also tied to <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> since, well, it is a supplement tied to it the same way that <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i> or <i>The Chicago Folio</i> is tied to <i>Chicago by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Opening Fiction: <i>Second Best Smile</i></b><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Summary</b>: <i>Second-Best Smile</i> is an interesting story about the character <b>Baptiste</b>, who is a member of the <b>Nephilim</b> cult. A Tremere belonging to the [b]Church of Set/b] is chasing down his ex-ghoul.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This is a pretty good opening fiction for <i>Children of the Blood</i>. It shows a rather petty bit of politicking between two members of cults and yet still pretty interesting in how it's done. In the end, the cultists are all looking for a sense of community in the World of Darkness and that means that the actual beliefs of the sects are less important than their ability to sell themselves to the locals. Thus, a member of the Church of Set can end up joining the Nephilim just because he's looking for his ex-girlfriend. We also see just how sick and twisted the Nephilim are as Baptiste skins her for a tattoo to frame.<br /> <br /> Because ART baby.<br /> <br /> I should note the Nephilim have really managed to take off as a concept as one of the Renegade free adventures, <i>Midnight Kiss</i>, is based around them. Given Michael and Mary the Black are acquainted with Baali in <i>Beckett's jyhad diary</i>, you could easily tie to the cult's resurgence with the now-no-longer-being-mentioned Bloodline. After all, what is more Baali-like than covering the face of utter evil in great beauty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T21:39:15-08:00","id":1529799,"title":"","content":"Now if we could just get the writers to remember the fact that you can buy a thermal imaging camera attachment for smart phones on Amazon for about $100, then perhaps the setting and the mechanics might advance rather than jogging in place and simply remixing the same old stuff.<br /> <br /> My point being that it doesn't matter if the elders are still present like in V20 or otherwise engaged like in V5, or if the xp and power accumulation for a character build is scaled up or down. The core vampire society design has not evolved since the first edition introduced the anarchs and the sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-31T21:49:56-08:00","id":1529801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529799#post1529799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if we could just get the writers to remember the fact that you can buy a thermal imaging camera attachment for smart phones on Amazon for about $100, then perhaps the setting and the mechanics might advance rather than jogging in place and simply remixing the same old stuff.<br /> <br /> My point being that it doesn't matter if the elders are still present like in V20 or otherwise engaged like in V5, or if the xp and power accumulation for a character build is scaled up or down. The core vampire society design has not evolved since the first edition introduced the anarchs and the sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thermal imaging camera that shows someone not showing up is malfunctioning rather than proving the existence of vampires, though. Because vampires don't exist and anyone who points to them doing so because of one is a lunatic. But I come from the school of thought that VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE should always reflect our world because it's about the metaphor of the super rich manipulating our lives from behind the scenes and the punks who oppose them. Gothic Punk is the sibling of cyberpunk and the player characters are meant to &quot;stick it to the man.&quot; It's not about providing a literal representation of an alternate fantasy world but just a politically charged metaphor.<br /> <br /> Once vampires exist out in the open, it's not <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> anymore or our world plus vampires.<br /> <br /> I admit, though, I may be biased as I'd not play <i>Shadow Run </i>but will play <i>Cyberpunk 2020</i>.<br /> <br /> I also think V:TM deserves credit for constantly updating the politics of its setting. The Anarchs have dramatically changed from 1st Edition and so have the Sabbat. I may not always like the settings changes but it's certainly grown and differentiated as a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T07:31:40-08:00","id":1529815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529801#post1529801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thermal imaging camera that shows someone not showing up is malfunctioning rather than proving the existence of vampires, though. Because vampires don't exist and anyone who points to them doing so because of one is a lunatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I come from the logistical school of thought rather than the thematic school of thought. A thermal imaging camera won't do much for breaking the masquerade, though it is hard to argue that the sensor is broken when you it shows singular room temperature bodies moving about in a crowd of normal temperature beings. The easy access to that sort of technology, along with other advancements means that vampires have to hide from such technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529801#post1529801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I come from the school of thought that VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE should always reflect our world because it's about the metaphor of the super rich manipulating our lives from behind the scenes and the punks who oppose them. Gothic Punk is the sibling of cyberpunk and the player characters are meant to &quot;stick it to the man.&quot; It's not about providing a literal representation of an alternate fantasy world but just a politically charged metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtM isn't about the super rich, this is proven by the fact that the Backgrounds used to represent such power are so underdeveloped and there are few systems centered around such stats. VtM is about the banality of existence in a world that is a shade darker than our own. It is the story of those who are willing to use what power they have at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> Also part of my original point is that a thermal sensor is now cheap enough technology that for the price of a AAA video game premium edition, anyone can scan a bar, movie theater, restaurant, etc and pick out cainites. In fact part of this comes from a little research I did recently where I tried to figure out exactly what would be needed to be a hunter equipment wise, and with the exception of a gun and bullet proof vest, everything you could want is available on Amazon for less than $2,000 which makes the barrier for entry horrifyingly low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529801#post1529801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once vampires exist out in the open, it's not <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> anymore or our world plus vampires.<br /> <br /> I admit, though, I may be biased as I'd not play <i>Shadow Run </i>but will play <i>Cyberpunk 2020</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comments are not to suggest that VtM should become Shadow Run, but instead they are to point out that the setup needs to change to avoid becoming Shadow Run. For vampires to operate in first world cities with modern technology and infrastructure, both the social structure and behavior would need to change.<br /> <br /> A quick example would be the idea that vampires hunt to feed every night as a default behavior while some others have Herds or maintain animal livestock. This might work is rural areas without city camera surveillance and access to facial identification databases. But in the big cities where vampires are supposed to lurk it would be far too risky to hunt unless as a last resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T09:56:26-08:00","id":1529822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529815#post1529815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My comments are not to suggest that VtM should become Shadow Run, but instead they are to point out that the setup needs to change to avoid becoming Shadow Run. For vampires to operate in first world cities with modern technology and infrastructure, both the social structure and behavior would need to change.<br /> <br /> A quick example would be the idea that vampires hunt to feed every night as a default behavior while some others have Herds or maintain animal livestock. This might work is rural areas without city camera surveillance and access to facial identification databases. But in the big cities where vampires are supposed to lurk it would be far too risky to hunt unless as a last resort.</div> </div> </div> </div>The larger question is, &quot;Does this make the game more fun for players?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is not being sarcastic but simply asking the Doylst answer that whether or not it is better for any changes to the campaign world in how they impact player enjoyment and agency. It was actually addressed in ANARCHS UNBOUND that the Red Question made it impossible for the government to track the Anarchs on the internet using magic. It was a hand wave but one designed to deal with the larger issues of changing technology.<br /> <br /> One that V5 obviously went a different route for.<br /> <br /> Other solutions include maybe not including the Delerium or that vampires now all have the Blush of Life due to a changing of the blood.<br /> <br /> What is the best way to keep up with changing technology and assumptions without compromising the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T11:54:44-08:00","id":1529831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529822#post1529822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The larger question is, &quot;Does this make the game more fun for players?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is not being sarcastic but simply asking the Doylst answer that whether or not it is better for any changes to the campaign world in how they impact player enjoyment and agency. It was actually addressed in ANARCHS UNBOUND that the Red Question made it impossible for the government to track the Anarchs on the internet using magic. It was a hand wave but one designed to deal with the larger issues of changing technology.<br /> <br /> One that V5 obviously went a different route for.<br /> <br /> Other solutions include maybe not including the Delerium or that vampires now all have the Blush of Life due to a changing of the blood.<br /> <br /> What is the best way to keep up with changing technology and assumptions without compromising the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>The simple answer is modularity rather than strict adherence to out-dated design concepts. This would allow the most amount of people to run games that suit their preferences without needing to home-brew or house rules huge swathes of the material.<br /> <br /> Consider how vampire societies are portrayed in other media/settings. Seraph of the End portrayed an underground vampire city which the humans had no clue about with a full hierarchy and laws. Conversely the movie Priest had vampires living in hives more akin to xenomorphs. Warhammer Fantasy has whole undead nations to play with.<br /> <br /> VtM largely suggests that every city that has vampires is owned by a faction, who have a diverse population representing most if not all clans. But never really accounts for the fact that vampires are supposed to be a low population critter, like a major city has one or two coteries worth of vampires. Also why in the world would a clan stake a claim on a city and then let others setup shop even if they belonged to the same faction?<br /> <br /> A city run by Nagaraja would probably have a vampire society more along the lines of the movie Midnight Meat Train than something VtM considers a normal city. So much of VtMs vampire society is made to create conflict, it is intentionally designed to create storyhooks, rather than creating functional vampire societies that are distinct from each other.<br /> <br /> As technology advances, vampires and their society will have to adjust, which in turn creates new things to squabble over and new factions to form. In an advanced technology culture do vampires have to retreat to third world countries or rural areas which have that level of infrastructure? Alternatively do the vampires stop trying to hide in human society and simply create underground cities with the factions being more political than armed forces? All of that can maintain the same themes that VtM has and falls in line with its history as already written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T14:08:45-08:00","id":1529835,"title":"","content":"This is something that we been trying to work around CTPhipps in regards to rapidly advancing technologies. We all play 150+ year old Kindred and we thought going old school in regards to communications such as drop sites, coded phrases in newspapers or graffiti or front people whom we have ghouled or we have a Nosferatu who has built up an investigative agency and we sometimes use his services to get messages across to reduce our presence online. We might create a version of Schrektnet later in the game and right now it's a work in progress. In addition having your fingers in a courior agency can help with advance technologies by having cut outs to serve as your agents to ferry goods and services across the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-02-2024, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-01T17:48:11-08:00","id":1529838,"title":"","content":"Short version; is this book worth getting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T08:09:56-08:00","id":1529855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529838#post1529838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short version; is this book worth getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not essential but it has a bunch of really fantastic NPCs that can be inserted into most chronicles since they're not tied to any specific place for the most part and are not very disruptive to campaigns.<br /> <br /> The one exception being the Prince of Coppenhagen who has a cool Nosferatu look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T12:44:23-08:00","id":1529863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529838#post1529838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short version; is this book worth getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want more story ideas or non player characters to add into the mix, then It's probably worth your time and money. Myself I probably won't buy Blood Sigils as I have no real interest in Blood Sorcery but some of my mates might pick it up for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T14:40:13-08:00","id":1529866,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of Blood part 2</b><br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> <br /> The introduction to <i>Children of Blood</i> more or less just explains what the book is and isn't. It is a supplement to <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> but not all of the characters are cultists. In fact, quite a few of them were actually characters that weren't fully detailed in <i>Let the Streets Run Red</i> and <i>Chicago by Night</i>. I don't hold this against the book at all but am glad that the people at OPP managed to get the room to be able to detail all of the wonderful NPCs as well as characters they wanted to detail even if they had to spread it across multiple books.<br /> <br /> It also says that you have permission to change these characters up as you see fit for your chronicle. This shouldn't need to be said but, well, a lot of Storytellers are antsy about breaking canon and this works well for it.<br /> <br /> The first section of the book will be the main part of the series, <b>Believers and Charlatans</b> that contains our collection of oddball NPCs. BTW, they're called SPCs in the book and while I understand brand identity, I just can't get my brain to switch over and call them the new adage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T15:00:49-08:00","id":1529869,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of the Blood #3: Florian Ribiero</b><br /> <br /> <img width=\"451\" height=\"539\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/48sXcsV.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/48sXcsV.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/48sXcsV.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: NPC<br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b>: A mathematical genius who sees God as a fundamental pattern to the universe and was Embraced by a Toreador. He was shattered by the existence of the supernatural, in part because it threw off all of his equations, and has since sought out Roger de Camden for secrets of the Mithraic mysteries.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Personal anecdote: I am a religious person but if you asked me to describe my religious beliefs, you would swiftly go down a rabbit hole starting with Star Wars' The Force, then being influenced by Hinduism, pantheism, and Spinoza's concept of the universe as a fundamental collection of infinite substance that we are all a part of. For my belief system, I jokingly refer to myself as a Christian Jedi and for a more serious belief system, I believe in a unification between reality and the divine that defies conventional explanation. If I wasn't so shit at mathematics, I would have probably been a decent Order of Hermes applicant but certainly would be able to slide into the Celestial Choir but they'd probably kick me to the curb for the Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> Which is to say I fucking love Florian Ribiero. He's a fantastic character and if he was written by Matthew Dawkins <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> (which I strongly expect to be the case) then he's my second favorite character in the book before his OTHER creation that I know was by him. This is notably higher praise than it sounds due to the fact that I made a couple of characters in the book. He's a character that fits perfectly into the World of Darkness but could have very easily have fallen into any number of other groups or Clans. Had circumstances been different, he might have been Embraced by the Tremere or Awakened as any number of other Traditions. Dude would have probably been an annoying addition to the Arcanum and having to deal with the fact he's surrounded by people who believe in, SCOFF, ghosts (and annoyed they exist).<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, Florian wants the universe to make sense and the fact is that the World of Darkness doesn't make sense. The real world doesn't make sense either, which is why real science is based around coming up with theories to explain away the parts that show why our current theories are inconveniently wrong. It's a matter of faith for him but he has no belief in a personal God and would probably explain why such an idea is ludicrous to a guy who can maybe talk to Gaia. He's joined the Cult of Mithras to try to work out some of these issues but I fear that it is the absolute worst sort of place for him because he's seeking a way to depersonalize God and reality in a group that very much has a personal relationship with their god. I fear he has to get out of Edinburgh before Mithras shows up (or is resurrected) and he gets himself killed trying to tell his fellow cultists the dude is &quot;just&quot; another vampire.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of places Florian's story could go from him getting deeper into the mysteries of Mithras, deciding he really wants to be something like a Nephilim instead (which is a later move since Michael is also a real being--and possibly Baali now), or trying to learn Blood Sorcery. He would either suck royally at magic or find the kind of power/insight that would potentially make him a massive threat to others. It would really depend on whether or not he learned it from a Banu Haqim or Tremere mentor, really.<br /> <br /> Also, I appreciate the fact that Florian is a gay man in a relationship with his sire with no sign of the angst that other games would normally put on it or big to do. Florian isn't even THAT in love with his sire or traumatized by events. They had a relationship, it was good, and now they've sort of drifted apart. It's a nice aversion to the usual V:TM melodrama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T15:19:58-08:00","id":1529872,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of Blood #4: Landon Dankworth AKA &quot;Father Christian Patriot&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <img width=\"304\" height=\"363\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VJuh0G3.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/VJuh0G3.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/VJuh0G3.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: NPC<br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b>: A Thin Blood radio host who is everything wrong with America or the guy telling you everything wrong with America. He is also ruler of his own town.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I love Father Christian Patriot more than most of Matthew Dawkins' creations because I hate Landon more than any other character in Vampire: The Masquerade. That include Balthazar, Lodin, Modius, and many other classic villains of the setting. I may have gotten way more use out of them than others but I've inserted the character's radio shows in the background of numerous games (they're set in Tampa, Florida after all) as well as done a decent couple of adventures about shutting him down.<br /> <br /> He fills that &quot;You sit in an O'Tolley's dining room&quot; or &quot;you fill up your gas at an Endron gas station&quot; role that helps flesh out the setting. My players share a collective Rush Limbaugh and Alex Jones trauma that makes it so none of us want to hear THEM in the background of stories but can grit their teeth at the Father Christian Patriot show. He's the perfect sort of character to also comment on the local occult news in an annoying way. When the players finally investigated his hometown, it was a culimination of numerous appearances in the background.<br /> <br /> The book notably has a sidebar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PLAYING WITH PREJUDICE<br /> <br /> A character such as Father Christian Patriot can be<br /> played up or down to the extent the players of your<br /> Vampire: The Masquerade game enjoy. Bear in mind<br /> that when invoking characters such as he, humor is<br /> one natural outcropping, as many people find comfort<br /> in mocking such bigotry, while hatred or upset<br /> is another. His views, and the views of many of his<br /> followers, are abhorrent. Therefore, it is vital for the<br /> Storyteller to check with the players before utilizing<br /> a character like this to that extent. If the players and<br /> Storyteller don\u2019t want an antagonist like Dankworth<br /> spewing his prejudicial bile, then he can focus entirely<br /> on his misguided pride, be adjusted to suit the<br /> story, or be replaced by a different antagonist. </div> </div> </div>I think this is good advice and I admit whenever I do my snippets of the Father Christian Patriot show, I tend to be a lot more circumspect than I would when referring to real people. The Hollywood elites, West Coast liberals, and THEM (you know who THEM are). As part of the &quot;humor&quot;, I also have him liberally mention vampires because his audience assumes he's speaking in code. I can't do anything about the real Alex Jones but we can certainly do something about Landon Dankworth, the discount Florida version.<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure Hook</b>: I actually combined Landon Dankworth with <b>Out for Blood</b> the interactive novel that also has a radio show run by a Kindred in a small town. In my combination universe, Landon is the childe of <b>Amanda Chastain</b> who is the one funding his growing Right Wing talk show. It makes an interesting twist to have him be the puppet of someone who looks like Ms. Orange County 1957.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"400\" height=\"304\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/57D1KLR.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/57D1KLR.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/57D1KLR.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-02T21:30:48-08:00","id":1529881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529835#post1529835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that we been trying to work around CTPhipps in regards to rapidly advancing technologies. We all play 150+ year old Kindred and we thought going old school in regards to communications such as drop sites, coded phrases in newspapers or graffiti or front people whom we have ghouled or we have a Nosferatu who has built up an investigative agency and we sometimes use his services to get messages across to reduce our presence online. We might create a version of Schrektnet later in the game and right now it's a work in progress. In addition having your fingers in a courior agency can help with advance technologies by having cut outs to serve as your agents to ferry goods and services across the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games, I emphasize that the majority of the Masquerade heavy lifting is actually done by the humans themselves. Whenever someone suggests vampires are real, they will seek ANY other explanation for it before settling on it unless they were unbalanced beforehand.<br /> <br /> Which means that hunters are always a threat but rarely do they have to worry about the end of the Masquerade as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dead Beat by Jim Butcher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cCome on, Butters,\u201d I said. \u201cLook at history. How long did the scholarly institutions of civilization consider Earth to be the center of the universe? And when people came out with facts to prove that it wasn\u2019t, there were riots in the streets. No one wanted to believe that we all lived on an unremarkable little speck of rock in a quiet backwater of one unremarkable galaxy. The world was supposed to be flat, too, until people proved that it wasn\u2019t by sailing all the way around it. No one believed in germs until years and years after someone actually saw one. Biologists scoffed at tales of wild beast-men living in the mountains of Africa, despite eyewitness testimony to the contrary, and pronounced them an utter fantasy\u2014right up until someone plopped a dead mountain gorilla down on their dissecting table.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chewed on his lip and watched the streetlights. \u201cTime after time, history demonstrates that when people don\u2019t want to believe something, they have enormous skills of ignoring it altogether.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re saying that the entire human race is in denial,\u201d he said.<br /> <br /> \u201cMost of the time,\u201d I replied. \u201cIt\u2019s not a bad thing. It\u2019s just who we are. But the weird stuff doesn\u2019t care about that\u2014it keeps on happening. Every family\u2019s got a ghost story in it. Most people I\u2019ve talked to have had something happen to them that was impossible to explain. But that doesn\u2019t mean they go around talking about it afterward, because everyone knows that those kinds of things aren\u2019t real. If you start saying that they are, you get the weird looks and jackets with extra-long sleeves.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor everyone,\u201d he said, voice still skeptical. \u201cEvery time. They just keep quiet and try to forget it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTell you what, Butters. Let\u2019s drive down to CPD and you can tell them how you were just attacked by a necromancer and four zombies. How they nearly outran a speeding car and murdered a security guard who then got up and threw your desk across the room.\u201d I paused for a moment to let the silence stretch. \u201cWhat do you think they\u2019d do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d he said. He bowed his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cUnnatural things happen all the time,\u201d I said. \u201cBut no one talks about it. At least, not openly. The preternatural world is everywhere. It just doesn\u2019t advertise.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a perfect solution but it's something that does allow us, the ST, to comment on the nature of disinformation and a Post-Truth society. Can we prove vampires exist?<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Maybe we can also get the world to believe in global warming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T11:28:09-08:00","id":1529923,"title":"","content":"That is a good way to remember on how the Masquerade would benifit from humans not wanting to know what is out there and staying safe. It reminds me of the Fermi Paradox when it comes to aliens CTPhipps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T23:01:28-08:00","id":1529965,"title":"","content":"<b>Children of the Blood part 5: Gloria &quot;Gums&quot; Flores<br /> <br /> <img width=\"443\" height=\"530\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/L77O9KI.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/L77O9KI.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/L77O9KI.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: NPC<br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b>: A LA beautiful beautician who has been Embraced by the Nosferatu and now wants to join the Nictuku.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Cleopatras are one of the darker concepts of the Nosferatu and we have them as people who are usually depicted as the vain, corrupt, or self-absorbed being punished in a kind of <i>Twilight Zone</i>-esque way. Here, Gloria is just a fairly decent woman from all accounts who happened to succeed with her cosmetics business before being horribly turned by a careless sire.<br /> <br /> Gloria has been understandably devastated by this horrifying action but it lacks the usual &quot;community&quot; of the Nosferatu where the Embraced person is welcomed into their oddball community. Their old life may be over but they are now part of a much-stranger community. At least, that's how I normally see the Nosferatu going on. Here, she seems painfully isolated and is now looking for a way to get revenge on her entire clan.<br /> <br /> One of the more interesting plot threads in <i>Forbidden Religions</i> was the possible retcon about the Nictuku. We know from <i>To Grandmother's House We Go</i> that they were supposed to be real but they've never quite made much sense within the game world. There's supposedly one Nosferatu 4th generation that wasn't one of their ranks that escaped Absimilard's Blood Bonding and that's why he's hunting them all down. However, Baba Yaga is a 4th generation that was clearly up against dear old dad but doesn't seem to be the progenitor of all Nosferatu. Indeed, some Nosferatu believed she was a Nictuku.<br /> <br /> Now, this clearly only matters to lore junkies but the <b>The Withered Ones</b> cult is a bunch of Nosferatu who hunt down other members of their Clan in order to impress the Nictuku. However, what I felt was being implied by the supplement is that the Withered Ones might BE the Nictuku. They're a bunch of crazy cultists worshiping the Boogeyman and there is no such thing as the Nictuku. It's always been just manifestations of their self-loathing. Maybe the Nosferatu who killed Baba Yaga was just a rival or one or her child (or Absimilard himself).<br /> <br /> I will say I have a small disappointment with Gloria. This seemed a great opportunity to tie her to one of the BLOODLINES characters. Either Gary Golden or Imalia could have been her sire and it would have gave the character a bit more continuity with the LA Nosferatu community. I love those kind of connections, though. On the other hand, I like both characters even if Imalia is a bit on the evil side herself. Gloria's sire was particularly cruel and arbitrary even by Nosferatu standards.<br /> <br /> In any case, she's a great Nosferatu and one that I very much enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T12:31:57-08:00","id":1529976,"title":"","content":"Getting embraced into the Nosferatu clan is a fate worse then death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T13:14:20-08:00","id":1529982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529976#post1529976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting embraced into the Nosferatu clan is a fate worse then death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that much more than other vampire clans.<br /> <br /> At least when you get the right levels of Obfuscate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T15:29:35-08:00","id":1529985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529976#post1529976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting embraced into the Nosferatu clan is a fate worse then death.</div> </div> </div> </div>A while back, I ran a one off game called &quot;The Unlucky&quot; for my group which was basically a game where the coterie is a mish mash of the sub-optimal builds to see how the players could work with it. Pretty much all of the worst vampire weaknesses are either appearance problems or feeding problems.<br /> <br /> Salubri Antitribu on path of humanity got complicated quickly when feeding.<br /> Gargoyles don't naturally have Obfuscate despite the 0-appearance issue.<br /> Ventrue on the path of humanity with a feeding restriction of 15 years old or younger only.<br /> <br /> Yet none of those caused the level of emotional upheaval from a &quot;play as yourself game&quot;, one of the players rolled a Brujah on the random embrace result and ended up having a frenzy at home.... family pushes buttons like no other and Brujah tend to make button pushers into paste. RPing the clean up, body disposal, and calling in a friendly ventrue to memory adjust people who knew the family more or less cemented in my mind that the Brujah clan weakness flies under the radar for how bad it can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T16:16:00-08:00","id":1529987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529985#post1529985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A while back, I ran a one off game called &quot;The Unlucky&quot; for my group which was basically a game where the coterie is a mish mash of the sub-optimal builds to see how the players could work with it. Pretty much all of the worst vampire weaknesses are either appearance problems or feeding problems.<br /> <br /> Salubri Antitribu on path of humanity got complicated quickly when feeding.<br /> Gargoyles don't naturally have Obfuscate despite the 0-appearance issue.<br /> Ventrue on the path of humanity with a feeding restriction of 15 years old or younger only.<br /> <br /> Yet none of those caused the level of emotional upheaval from a &quot;play as yourself game&quot;, one of the players rolled a Brujah on the random embrace result and ended up having a frenzy at home.... family pushes buttons like no other and Brujah tend to make button pushers into paste. RPing the clean up, body disposal, and calling in a friendly ventrue to memory adjust people who knew the family more or less cemented in my mind that the Brujah clan weakness flies under the radar for how bad it can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;you frenzy and kill your mortal family&quot; is one I've pulled as a Storyteller myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T23:13:37-08:00","id":1530008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1529976#post1529976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting embraced into the Nosferatu clan is a fate worse then death.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is true, during the nights following the Embrace (or instantly, depends) the fledgeling's body painfully warps and twists as ther Clan Curse took hold and the chance of a Nosferatu dying in the process of the Embrace is higher than in other Clans and many emerge as simple brutes, their brains damaged and incapable of higher thought or basic survival skills, the Clan itself is supportive and as close as it cn gets; the Nosferatu strongly stress clan loyalty over almost everything else. Given their hideous appearance, they depend heavily on clan support structures for everything from havens to food, Broods are generally gerontocratic, with the eldest Nosferatu setting policy and guiding the youngest.<br /> The transformation is horrible and last forever, but if you can live with your new look as a vampire, you are on a good start and the best chances to survive<br /> Actually the Book fo Nod have a passage on this &quot;In any Jyhad, the Nosferatu are the first to die.&quot; but this is the bigest and most amusing mistranslation of all time, the correct translation according Backett and other renowed Nodist and the whole assamite clan is: &quot;In any Jyhad, the Nosferatu are the first to <i>disappear</i>.&quot;<br /> If you ever expect trouble to strike your city, keep a close eye on the Nosferatu: when they vanish down their boltholes and pull them shut, follow their example. They are the Cainite world's greatest survivors, and they can see a threat clearly before anyone else has more than a vague sense of unease.<br /> <br /> Getting Embraced in to a Lasombra?<br /> Now that is indeed a fate worse than death, because it literally expect you to become someone else what and who you were as a human!<br /> Even the Baali gives yo ua choice and you have to dig your way to a heart filled with your would-be Sire's blood in a sacrifical well filled with rotten corpses, but it is your choice.<br /> But for the Lasombra?<br /> It is common for the Keeper to decide to 'test' that mortal to see if they can rise to the occasion, or if they will instead crumble under the weight of the Lasombra's attention. These tests will feel like the victim's life is falling apart, as they lose their job and opportunities, become alienated from friends and family, or even suffer great physical harm at the hands of the monster. How they react is what matters, whether they become strong or reveal themselves to be pitiful. That is what decides whether they are left in the ruins, or brought into the night.<br /> Immagine, you have a perfect life, job, whife, everything is okay, sure, you were maybe ruthless, fought against the odds, survive dangerous situations, and exist at the pinnacle of excellence.. but that was what draw the eyes of the Lasombra upon you<br /> And it is <i>not enough</i>!<br /> Your life, for some mysterious reason, slowly or quickly fell apart. No matter what you do, everything around you crumbles and you are powerless to do anything against it no matter how hard you try - and fully expected to try to stop it, not just accept it, becasue that would mean, you are a weakling - and when you finally hit rock bottom... you discover, hey, there is still something under it and that hell awaits you!<br /> THEN maybe, if you are &quot;worthy&quot;, your Sire reveal itself to reward you the Embrace and more often than not, reveal, he was the reason behind your troubles<br /> And you find yourself in the company of social dawinist predators and ruthless social climbers who seek power and authority to prove themselves better than others<br /> Who you were when your Sire noticed you are long destroyed and rebuilt from the ruins of your old life and self<br /> The Lasombra and the Sith have many things in comon except the Sith are way more humane and nicer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T02:41:22-08:00","id":1530012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1530008#post1530008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it is true, during the nights following the Embrace (or instantly, depends) the fledgeling's body painfully warps and twists as ther Clan Curse took hold and the chance of a Nosferatu dying in the process of the Embrace is higher than in other Clans and many emerge as simple brutes, their brains damaged and incapable of higher thought or basic survival skills, the Clan itself is supportive and as close as it cn gets; the Nosferatu strongly stress clan loyalty over almost everything else. Given their hideous appearance, they depend heavily on clan support structures for everything from havens to food, Broods are generally gerontocratic, with the eldest Nosferatu setting policy and guiding the youngest.<br /> The transformation is horrible and last forever, but if you can live with your new look as a vampire, you are on a good start and the best chances to survive<br /> Actually the Book fo Nod have a passage on this &quot;In any Jyhad, the Nosferatu are the first to die.&quot; but this is the bigest and most amusing mistranslation of all time, the correct translation according Backett and other renowed Nodist and the whole assamite clan is: &quot;In any Jyhad, the Nosferatu are the first to <i>disappear</i>.&quot;<br /> If you ever expect trouble to strike your city, keep a close eye on the Nosferatu: when they vanish down their boltholes and pull them shut, follow their example. They are the Cainite world's greatest survivors, and they can see a threat clearly before anyone else has more than a vague sense of unease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating observation on the Nosferatu versus Lasombra and that's actually the main point I had about Gums' entry above. She doesn't seem to have any support or friendship or aid from her fellow Nosferatu in LA's warren. Which is a sharp contrast to Imalia, a woman also embraced for the exact same reason by her sire in BLOODLINES and for apparently far more &quot;justified&quot; reasons of being an objectively terrible person.<br /> <br /> So it's no wonder that Gums wants to join the Niktuku in order to destroy her fellow Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T05:00:10-08:00","id":1530020,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> Living as they do in places many would consider to be Hell, there is a long tradition of the Nosferatu offering help to others like them.<br /> The Nosferatu tend to embrace two classes of people: first are those for whom the Embrace is a step up<br /> The second class are those for whom the Embrace is a step down, such as beauty queens or people from privileged backgrounds. Nosferatu are notorious for revenge Embraces, and the resulting Cleopatras often lead miserable lives within the clan, thats true<br /> While some Nosferatu create Cleopatras as punishment this is not only the case<br /> But it is the because of the Cleoptara in question, not the Clan... as you said, Imalia was embraced for the exact same reason by her sire but she managed to find her place<br /> They are the classic case of &quot;God helps those who help themselves' in a sense<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T11:30:53-08:00","id":1530045,"title":"","content":"Yes I wouldn't be to shocked if a number of Lasombra sires met a final death at the hands of one of there childer when they learned that he or she was the mastermind of all you lost. All the clans have there drawbacks but being a member of the Nosferatu or Lasombra clan would be at the top for clans that you don't want to draw attention from at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-05-2024, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T13:36:51-08:00","id":1530051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529766-wir-children-of-the-blood?p=1530008#post1530008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THEN maybe, if you are &quot;worthy&quot;, your Sire reveal itself to reward you the Embrace and more often than not, reveal, he was the reason behind your troubles<br /> And you find yourself in the company of social dawinist predators and ruthless social climbers who seek power and authority to prove themselves better than others<br /> Who you were when your Sire noticed you are long destroyed and rebuilt from the ruins of your old life and self<br /> The Lasombra and the Sith have many things in comon except the Sith are way more humane and nicer</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that from the perspective of a person not brought up in that sort of environment, it is horrific, but if that was your mortal life to begin with, it is Tuesday. But this in turn begs the question of would a Lasombra even bother embracing someone who isn't natively accustomed to that sort of darwinist existence in the first place?<br /> <br /> I could see a couple Lasombra making a bet like an infernal version of &quot;My Fair Lady&quot; where they see who is better at training the lesser beings up to their standards. But I don't see that being the default behavior for making childer.<br /> <br /> Though it does make me chuckle when I think that modern day people consider the behavior of what would be a strict martial arts instructor or a British school master to be in the same ballpark as Sith or other capital &quot;E&quot; evil bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T14:00:33-08:00","id":1530053,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of the Lasombra &quot;Social Darwinist&quot; philosophy is that it is there to avoid Embracing Jacon Schumpeters. If anyone remembers that character, Lodin Embraced him because he was worried he'd made rivals by Embracing Ballard and Al Capone who were becoming too powerful as well as independent. Lodin assumed he was Embracing an up and coming financial genius. When, in fact, Jacob Schumpeter was actually rich solely because he was insider trading with the help of his father in law (which was already a problem because Jacob was abusing his wife).<br /> <br /> By taking away all of their mortal ties and wealth, the Lasombra wants to see if the Fledgling is capable of bouncing back on their own merit. Which is useful because you can't rely on inherited wealth or other benefits in Kindred society.<br /> <br /> Also, much like the Sith, the Lasombra disdain loyalty. If you're NOT taking a shot at your sire then you've failed as a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Memb